@startuml redis-03-startup-order
!include _style.iuml
title Sentinel cluster startup — the order is not negotiable

participant "SentinelContainer\nFactory" as F
participant "master" as M
participant "replica1..N" as R
participant "Docker API" as D
participant "sentinel1..M" as S

== 1 · master ==
F -> M ++: redis-server --protected-mode no
M --> F --: log: "**Ready to accept connections**"
note right of M #12305a
  Wait on the *log line*, not the port.
  An open port proves nothing.
end note

== 2 · replicas ==
F -> R ++: redis-server --replicaof redis-master 6379
R -> M: PSYNC (full sync: RDB + backlog)
R --> F --: log: "**MASTER <-> REPLICA sync: Finished with success**"
note right of R #12305a
  PING would answer during RDB load —
  and return **-LOADING** to your test.
  Only this line means "dataset present".
end note

== 3 · address resolution ==
F -> D ++: inspect(master).NetworkSettings
D --> F --: **172.x.x.x** (internal IP)
note over F #3a2c12
  The IP — not the alias. This address is
  gossiped to every Sentinel and handed
  to every client. See FIG-04 / FIG-05.
end note

== 4 · sentinels ==
F -> S ++: printf sentinel.conf && redis-server … --sentinel
note right of S
  port 26379
  sentinel monitor mymaster <ip> 6379 **2**
  sentinel down-after-milliseconds mymaster **2000**
  sentinel parallel-syncs mymaster 1
  sentinel failover-timeout mymaster **5000**
end note
S --> F --: exec ok: redis-cli -p 26379 SENTINEL master mymaster

== 5 · stabilisation ==
F -> F: sleep 2 s
note right of F #3a1c1c
  Pragmatic floor, not a guarantee.
  Redis docs: a Sentinel acquires the other
  Sentinels and replicas "within 10 seconds".
end note

F -> F: **SentinelCluster** handed to the test
@enduml
